  "name": "FACTOR - XIII (CLOT SOLUBILITY - FUNCTIONAL) QUALITATIVE",
  "code": "1543",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong data-start=\"74\" data-end=\"117\">Factor XIII (Fibrin-stabilizing factor)</strong> is a critical enzyme in the final step of the coagulation cascade. It stabilizes the fibrin clot by cross-linking fibrin polymers, making the clot resistant to fibrinolysis. The <strong data-start=\"296\" data-end=\"320\">clot solubility test</strong> is a <strong data-start=\"326\" data-end=\"358\">qualitative functional assay</strong> used to assess Factor XIII activity.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Clot dissolves</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Abnormal</strong> &ndash; Suggests <strong>Factor XIII deficiency</strong> (usually &lt;5&ndash;10% activity)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Clot remains</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Normal</strong> &ndash; Indicates adequate Factor XIII function (&gt;10% activity)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1164\" data-end=\"1193\"><strong data-start=\"1168\" data-end=\"1193\">Clinical Significance</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1195\" data-end=\"1236\"><strong data-start=\"1200\" data-end=\"1234\">Decreased Factor XIII Activity</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1237\" data-end=\"1275\">May be <strong data-start=\"1244\" data-end=\"1258\">congenital</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1262\" data-end=\"1274\">acquired</strong>.</p>\n<ol data-start=\"1277\" data-end=\"1801\">\n<li data-start=\"1277\" data-end=\"1592\">\n<p data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1318\"><strong data-start=\"1280\" data-end=\"1317\">Congenital Factor XIII Deficiency</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1322\" data-end=\"1592\">\n<li data-start=\"1322\" data-end=\"1358\">\n<p data-start=\"1324\" data-end=\"1358\">Rare autosomal recessive disorder.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1362\" data-end=\"1592\">\n<p data-start=\"1364\" data-end=\"1388\">Bleeding may present as:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1394\" data-end=\"1592\">\n<li data-start=\"1394\" data-end=\"1440\">\n<p data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1440\">Umbilical stump bleeding (common early sign)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1446\" data-end=\"1493\">\n<p data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1493\">Intracranial hemorrhage (even without trauma)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1499\" data-end=\"1545\">\n<p data-start=\"1501\" data-end=\"1545\">Recurrent spontaneous miscarriage (in women)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1551\" data-end=\"1592\">\n<p data-start=\"1553\" data-end=\"1592\">Poor wound healing and keloid formation</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1594\" data-end=\"1801\">\n<p data-start=\"1597\" data-end=\"1633\"><strong data-start=\"1597\" data-end=\"1632\">Acquired Factor XIII Deficiency</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1637\" data-end=\"1801\">\n<li data-start=\"1637\" data-end=\"1801\">\n<p data-start=\"1639\" data-end=\"1655\">Can result from:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1661\" data-end=\"1801\">\n<li data-start=\"1661\" data-end=\"1705\">\n<p data-start=\"1663\" data-end=\"1705\">Autoantibodies (inhibitors) to Factor XIII</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1711\" data-end=\"1733\">\n<p data-start=\"1713\" data-end=\"1733\">Severe liver disease</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1739\" data-end=\"1749\">\n<p data-start=\"1741\" data-end=\"1749\">Leukemia</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1755\" data-end=\"1801\">\n<p data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1801\">Disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>",
